sc7731g-frame-linux
===================

No vendor firmware is included in this repository, and none ever will be.

The SC7731G frame needs four pieces of vendor firmware to work under Linux:

- the WCN co-processor's firmware (Wi-Fi and Bluetooth), Spreadtrum/Unisoc's;
- the Wi-Fi calibration block, built from the vendor's calibration files;
- the Bluetooth PSKEY block, built from the vendor's configuration file and,
  for its Bluetooth address, the frame's own serial number;
- the GSL1680 touch controller's firmware, Silead's, as compiled into the
  frame's Android kernel.

None of them is ours to redistribute, and some carry per-unit data. So this
repository carries only tools that extract them from the frame you own
(firmware/extract.sh, tools/), the SHA-256 checksums of the inputs and
outputs we tested with (firmware/SHA256SUMS), and the description of any
patch applied to them (firmware/patches/). The PSKEY is built on the frame
itself at boot (rootfs/usr/lib/sc7731g-bt/pskey.sh). The same goes for the
vendor's U-Boot and boot ROM: they stay on the frame, untouched and not
copied here.

Register layouts, struct offsets and command ids in the drivers and docs
were learned from the frame's own firmware and from Samsung's GPL kernel
source for the SM-G531H (the same SoC), for interoperability.

Licences
--------

- kernel/*.c, kernel/*.h, kernel/mach-sprd/, kernel/patches/: GPL-2.0-only
